"""ui — live UI engine for build-ios prototypes.

The app's UI is JSON in design/. The app running in the iOS Simulator
hot-reloads it (~0.2 s), so a UI change never needs a rebuild. This tool makes
those changes fast and safe for people and for small, fast models:

  ./ui context              compact map of the current screen (what a model reads)
  ./ui apply '<ops>'        validate + apply id-addressed edits, wait for the render
  ./ui undo                 revert the last apply
  ./ui pick                 tap an element in the Simulator -> prints its id
  ./ui ask "<request>"      one model call -> ops -> applied   (-n 3 for variants)
  ./ui next | prev | keep   cycle / keep variants from `ask -n`
  ./ui tune [id]            no-model fast lane: single keys nudge size/padding/color…
  ./ui chat                 interactive loop (fastest: keeps the model client warm)
  ./ui status | shot | stats | validate | reference
  ./ui eval                 accuracy + latency of the model on tools/evals.jsonl
  ./ui hook                 Claude Code hook entry point (see .claude/settings.json)

Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 error · 2 validation failed (hook) · 3 ESCALATE (needs Swift)

Ops reference: tools/REFERENCE.md. Core commands need only the python3 that
ships with macOS; `ask`/`chat` call Claude via the official anthropic SDK
(auto-run through `uv` when it isn't installed) or fall back to `claude -p`.
"""
